        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2013",
        "question_text": "<p>Under the <b>straight-line method</b> of depreciation, if an asset costs $20,000, has a residual value of $2,000, and a useful life of 5 years, what is the annual depreciation charge?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The straight-line depreciation formula is: <b>$(Cost - Residual Value) / Useful Life$</b>. Substituting the values: <b>$(20,000 - 2,000) / 5 = 3,600$</b>.</p>",
